#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# de_bruijn_sequence

#% text
# `de_bruijn_sequence(alphabet, m)` gives the lexicographically least cyclic sequence in which every word of length `m` over the alphabet occurs exactly once. The alphabet is a list, a string, or a number `k` meaning `0` to `k - 1`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
de_bruijn_sequence([0, 1], 3)
#% output
#= [0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1]

#% cell
de_bruijn_sequence(4, 2)
#% output
#= [0, 0, 1, 0, 2, 0, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1, 3, 2, 2, 3, 3]

#% cell
de_bruijn_sequence("abcd", 2)
#% output
#= "aabacadbbcbdccdd"

#% cell
length(de_bruijn_sequence(3, 4))
#% output
#= 81

